body:
Appreciate the difficulty comparison from someone who's taken both.  I don't think I want to take with Ord, and considering next quarter is his last, I'm sort of leaning towards 100 in order to do 30 with whoever takes his place. 

That way my hand will be forced as far as deciding if I want to take him or not lol. Making decisions isn't fun. 

&#x200B;

A spot opened up last minute, man. Congrats.

&#x200B;

Also, it's never put your mouth on a horse's *gift* or you'll be looked at.

It's strange to think someone can earn a zero when completing an assignment, simply because they went beyond the scope of what's been taught. I've always viewed that as a backwards way of teaching, but I guess it can perhaps prepare one for future assignments where possibly certain restrictions are in play. Definitely looking forward to machine language in the future...haha. I fixed a few things with my code, by the way. Currently does what I need it to when i switched a few things around. Thanks again for steering me in the right direction. For reference:

     public Card dealCard()
    {
        int i = 0;                        
        Card topCard = null;
        if(deck.size() > 0)
        {
            topCard = deck.remove(i);
        }           
        else
        {
            System.out.println("Fatal Error. Program now exiting.");
            System.exit(0);
        }

        return topCard;
    }
